We've already completed **13 iterations** — iteration #3 was done earlier. Here's what it covered:

**Iteration #3 (Completed) — Advanced Themes II:**
- **E1. Regime Detection & Regime-Aware Strategies** — 3-regime rule-based model (Bull/Crisis/Choppy); Conservative regime filter improved Calmar to 0.44
- **E2. Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP)** — Rolling 252d, rebal 21d: Sharpe 0.84, Calmar 0.35
- **E3. Factor Investing** — Momentum, Low Vol, Value, Quality; Equal-weight combo: Sharpe 0.74, Calmar 0.30; Low Vol best DD (-12%)
- **E4. Transaction-Cost-Aware Optimization** — Cost-aware optimizer produced Calmar 0.76 (best at the time)
- **E5. Multi-Horizon Signal Blending** — Didn't improve over single-horizon; added noise and turnover
- **E6. Stochastic Stress Testing** — GBM: Sharpe ~0.43; OU (mean-reverting): Sharpe -4.51 (momentum destroyed); Jump-Diffusion: Sharpe ~0.46

**Key Finding:** Momentum strategies fail catastrophically under strong mean-reversion (OU process). Stress testing reveals regime assumptions matter more than parameter tuning.

**Outputs:** `iter3_*.csv`, `iter3_*.png` in `/root/quant/`

